1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,080
Seven years of car payments? That's five grand you'll never see again.

2
00:00:04,660 --> 00:00:07,980
Same car, but you pick the monthly payment. Option one is one thousand seventy dollars.

3
00:00:09,780 --> 00:00:10,960
Option two? Only six seventy-four.

4
00:00:12,180 --> 00:00:14,280
Which one you picking? Yeah, the small one.

5
00:00:14,840 --> 00:00:18,020
You borrow about forty-four thousand seven hundred for a new car.

6
00:00:18,420 --> 00:00:20,540
That's the average new car loan, per Edmunds.

7
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,440
Now tap like if your car payment already hurts.

8
00:00:23,940 --> 00:00:28,340
The bank charges seven percent a year in interest. Basically, rent on money.

9
00:00:28,340 --> 00:00:31,100
Pay it off in four years, and the interest is about six thousand seven hundred.

10
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:36,380
Stretch it to seven years, and it's about ten— no, almost twelve thousand.

11
00:00:37,880 --> 00:00:41,200
Wait, so the cheap payment costs about five thousand three hundred more?

12
00:00:41,740 --> 00:00:45,400
Yep. Same car, same rate, three extra years of interest.

13
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:47,860
Send this to the friend whose payment is "only six seventy-four."

14
00:00:49,320 --> 00:00:52,620
At the typical wage, that's two hundred sixteen hours of work.

15
00:00:53,080 --> 00:00:55,680
And at nine percent? Seven-year interest hits almost fifteen thousand seven hundred.

16
00:00:57,760 --> 00:00:59,600
Follow if you'd rather see the receipt first.

17
00:01:00,080 --> 00:01:03,320
Oh, and when it's finally paid off, your car's seven years old.

18
00:01:03,800 --> 00:01:06,100
Low payment, high price. That's the trick.

19
00:01:06,560 --> 00:01:08,680
So be honest, how many years is your car loan?

